<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hartford, Connecticut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1636">1636</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hartford is the capital of the US state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>. It was founded in 1636 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-hooker">Thomas Hooker</a>, who came from Massachusetts, and with Windsor and Wethersfield it formed the Connecticut Colony, governed under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fundamental-orders-of-connecticut">Fundamental Orders</a> of 1639. It later became a centre of the insurance industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hartford-connecticut.jpg" alt="Hartford, Connecticut" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hartford,_CT_skyline_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
